1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,238
Here's a maths problem.

2
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:07,449
Mia has 3 times as many marbles as Ben.

3
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:11,986
Together, they have 24. How many does Ben have?

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,443
Tricky? Not the S.A.M way.

5
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:20,416
Step 1. Make it real.

6
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:25,590
1 block for Ben. 3 blocks for Mia.

7
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:29,881
Every block is the same size. That's the secret.

8
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:32,451
Step 2. Draw a picture.

9
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:37,549
Each block becomes a bar. We call it a unit.

10
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:40,959
All the units together make 24.

11
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:44,564
Step 3. Now the numbers.

12
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:48,452
4 units = 24

13
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,027
So 1 unit = 6

14
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:57,474
Ben has 6. Mia has 18.

15
00:00:58,250 --> 00:01:03,355
Concrete. Pictorial. Abstract. That's Singapore Maths.

16
00:01:06,250 --> 00:01:11,910
180+ students are already learning this way at J3 Mall.

17
00:01:12,250 --> 00:01:14,322
And S.A.M is growing.

18
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:19,663
New branches in Meydan and Al Barsha.

19
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:22,862
And AB Centre, opening soon.

20
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:27,869
S.A.M Singapore Maths. Come and see the bars.
